    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Seems that cupy's matmul computes with cublas gemm routines when ndim > 2. Cublas gemm routines support only floating-point or complex values, so `x @ y` above is computed in float32 then casted back to an integer. However, float32 in IEEE754 representation has only 24-bit precision, thus numbers equal to or larger than 2^24 = 16777216 lose some bits from LSB and get rounded.\r\n\r\n```py\r\n>>> np.int32(51307*327).astype('H')\r\n173\r\n>>> np.float32(51307*327).astype('H')\r\n172\r\n```",
    "created_at": "2022-05-14T05:37:55Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/cupy/cupy/issues/6715#issuecomment-1126646316",
